WEBVTT

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.290
<i>The Enoshima High School 
traditional match</i>

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:05.730
<i>for school representation has begun.</i>

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:10.200
<i>We the FC, still without 
the conductor named Araki,</i>

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.470
<i>faced off against the SC.</i>

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:15.450
<i>We all fought as hard 
as we could together,</i>

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.320
<i>but the SC was strong;</i>

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.450
<i>we were immediately pushed into a corner.</i>

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.670
<i>Still, we gritted our teeth and fought</i>

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:23.670
<i>and we somehow managed to 
score a goal against them,</i>

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:27.250
<i>but, after that, we were unable 
to break through the SC's lead.</i>

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.000
<i>All the while, the time left in 
the match continued to tick away.</i>

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:07.870
Goooal!

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:09.700
SC scores another goal.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:12.550
The score is now 3-1!

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:13.640
Damn it!

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.840
Not yet! It isn't over yet!

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.860
We'll have the last laugh!

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.920
Trailing by two goals,

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:23.020
FC is starting to feel the pressure.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.950
Coach, if things keep going...

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:32.890
I know. But don't panic.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:35.190
We still have an ace up our sleeve.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:36.210
What?

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.470
By ace, you don't mean...

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:43.440
We've been expecting you, King.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:46.270
Can you play for the last 20 minutes?

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:48.220
Obviously.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.270
That's why I've endured 
waiting in the stands.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:57.740
Just watch. 
The show's about to begin.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:02.240
Number 12, Endo, is substituted 
for number 10, Araki!

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:16.550
The magic show is about to begin.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:24.890
<b>Return Of The King</b>

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.850
Enoshima High FC announces 
a substitution.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:33.140
What do you know?! It's Araki!

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:34.560
Enoshima Broadcasting Club

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:34.560
Ladies and gentlemen, 
would you look at that?

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.020
In the match against SC last year,

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:40.140
he surprised the school 
with his magic-like plays.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:43.530
Number 10, Ryuichi Araki, has returned!

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.560
Whoa!

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:45.620
He lost weight.

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:48.120
He might be kinda hot, 
now that he's thin!

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.920
Did you know Araki-san would come?

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:00.880
Yes, we had discussed it.

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:06.300
Please!

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.650
Allow me to join the team!

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:09.500
I cannot.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.680
Do you think you can actually play

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:18.370
in a body weighed down like that?

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:20.320
Don't underestimate soccer.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:24.360
Go lose some weight.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:29.090
There are 10 days left 
until the match against SC.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:32.480
Go get in your best shape by then.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:35.000
If you can do that, 
I'll approve your return.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:40.250
Look at that physique.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:42.410
He managed to keep all his lean muscle

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:44.620
while dropping all his fat.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:46.870
Probably the result of careful dieting

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:49.040
and rigorous training.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:52.350
But why did you keep it a secret?

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.210
If he was on the bench the whole time,

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:59.190
everyone would depend on his presence.

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:03.110
"We have to win this 
match by ourselves."

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:04.500
I knew positive thoughts like that

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.180
would influence their playing.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:11.040
<i>This man really is amazing.</i>

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.550
Seriously, look who finally showed up.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:16.170
I'm sorry I made you worry, Mako.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:19.880
I'm counting on you, King.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:20.590
Yeah.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:22.920
Araki-san, you came for us.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:27.890
I have a big debt I need 
to repay to these guys.

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:37.200
The game will resume 
with SC's goal kick.

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:44.070
Araki, you're late.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:47.400
You won't be able to overcome a two 
goal deficit with the time left.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:49.870
You mean, if I hadn't shown up.

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:55.330
What can you do by yourself?

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.860
What's wrong, Sawamura-san?

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:04.300
Doesn't the SC prohibit dribbling 
for longer than five seconds?

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:07.260
<i>Man, this guy hasn't changed.</i>

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:09.790
<i>I'd pass it if I could, 
but I can't get an opening!</i>

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.530
<i>We have a two goal lead.</i>

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:16.520
<i>There's no need to force an attack.</i>

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:21.860
<i>Shoot!</i>

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.360
Got it!

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:27.190
Amazing! He intercepted it right away!

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.970
A first rate player responds to

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:30.410
the flow of the match

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:33.330
and takes advantage of his opponent's
 emotional state with his movements.

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:36.790
He was able to read Sawamura-kun's 
thoughts quite admirably.

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:42.470
What will the magician, 
Ryuichi Araki, pull out next?

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:45.210
He pushes into the SC's 
defense with his dribble.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.980
<i>Ladies and gentlemen...</i>

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.880
<i>We should probably score a goal, first.</i>

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.020
<i>Araki-san!</i>

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:08.240
Bring it, Araki!

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:19.320
What?

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:42.100
<i>R-Rabona?</i>

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.810
Goooal!

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:58.170
Only minutes after 
stepping onto the field,

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:00.870
FC's Ryuichi Araki scores a goal!

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:03.760
You're amazing, Araki!

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:04.830
So cool!

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.500
3 to 2!

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:09.760
Ryuichi Araki claims a goal 
with amazing skill!

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:13.340
The second row magician 
is finally back in full form!

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.830
You bastard.

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:16.930
You did it!

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:22.460
<i>Amazing. That was amazing, Araki-san.</i>

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:24.600
<i>The magic plays that inspired</i>

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.560
<i>Suguru-san are being realized.</i>

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.730
<i>One more goal. 
We can do it, definitely!</i>

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.190
I let my guard down.

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:35.250
He's cunning.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:39.850
As always, you never know 
what he's going to do.

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:41.250
Ryuichi Araki.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.700
Even so, we will win.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:47.070
We'll hold this one goal lead, 
no matter what.

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:47.960
Yes!

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:50.110
Araki-san, you're amazing.

00:08:50.110 --> 00:08:51.350
You idiot.

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:53.130
We're still down a goal.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.590
This is no time to celebrate.

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:57.810
Sorry, but I'm so happy.

00:08:57.810 --> 00:08:59.850
This time, it's your turn.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:00.560
What?

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:02.650
It takes two to create a pass

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:06.520
that tears down their 
iron defense, right?

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:08.480
Araki-san...

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:10.340
But, since the first half,

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:12.680
there's been something 
lacking in your plays.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.700
You set the stage.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:20.260
I'll direct.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.660
Let's put on an amazing show.

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:24.850
<i>Stage?</i>

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.380
I won't let you through!

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:43.720
Yukizo. Back up Mako.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:45.250
You're slowing down in the second half.

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:46.690
Okay.

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:47.440
Kaoru!

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.770
Uh... Yes?

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.020
Don't worry about the right side.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.130
Move to fill the spaces.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:55.030
Okay!

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:58.010
<i>He must have been watching 
me carefully the whole time,</i>

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:00.990
<i>to have noticed that I was 
only playing the right side.</i>

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:03.360
You there, with the spiky hair...

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:04.480
Yeah, what's up?

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:06.210
Not "what's up."

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:07.550
You can overlap on your defense,

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:09.170
but you're too slow to return.

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:12.220
The left side is wide open 
with a huge hole in it.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:14.700
If they send a pass out, 
get back immediately, got it?

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:16.880
Right. Sorry.

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:19.190
Precise directions.

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:21.190
He only just got on the field,

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:23.100
but it seems like he's been 
playing the whole time.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:25.870
Stay tight on Aizawa's mark.

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:27.980
Don't let him play in the 
penalty area anymore.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.310
Okay.

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:33.240
<i>Oda's getting all fired up, 
now that Araki's on the field.</i>

00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:35.780
<i>Not that I don't understand how he feels.</i>

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:42.830
Takase!

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:46.220
I'll take that.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:47.550
All right.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:50.600
Now that Araki-kun's back,

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:52.790
we're finally starting 
to look like the FC.

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:54.510
Kaoru!

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:01.340
Matoba!

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:14.260
FC pulls off a spectacular side 
change from right to left.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:16.960
The ball has passed to the overlapping

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:19.130
first year sideback, Nakatsuka Kota.

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:20.860
What will you do, Nakatsuka?

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:23.870
<i>I'll take it down the line.</i>

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:25.140
Kota!

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:29.750
<i>It's too soon to pass!</i>

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:34.250
Take it!

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:41.050
Kakeru!

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:43.650
That was a run-with-the-ball.

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:47.280
Trapping the ball and, 
rather than feinting,

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:49.030
moving the ball into the 
space you've created

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:51.020
and rushing forward is more effective

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:53.060
at slipping past the defender.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:56.960
<i>What do you think you're doing?</i>

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:59.490
<i>Is he planning on pushing 
through with his dribble?</i>

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:02.940
<i>Looks like he understood what I meant.</i>

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:04.700
<i>That's it. That's good.</i>

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.160
Don't let him through! Stop him!

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:13.340
<i>If you've really got what 
it takes to be the</i>

00:12:13.340 --> 00:12:15.290
<i>knight that Suguru said you would be,</i>

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:17.380
<i>then you can do it, Kakeru!</i>

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:22.550
<i>The thing that my plays lack...</i>

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:38.660
Unfortunately, the ball 
rebounds off the goal post!

00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:41.180
However, that was a 
spectacular middle shot

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:43.050
that clearly took the 
SC defense by surprise.

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:44.820
Number 9, Kakeru Aizawa.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:46.520
A powerful right from the penalty area

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:49.000
that doesn't seem to 
match his small figure.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.040
The SC had better not 
let their guard down.

00:12:51.970 --> 00:12:54.250
He can hit middle shots like that?

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:58.140
<i>He's bringing out his ranged weapons.</i>

00:12:58.140 --> 00:13:02.020
<i>It's not like Suguru's rocket middle,</i>

00:13:02.020 --> 00:13:03.470
<i>but it's not bad.</i>

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:07.430
<i>He may be able to set 
the stage with that.</i>

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:10.470
FC still has a chance.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.920
The corner kicker is none 
other than that man,

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:14.440
Ryuichi Araki.

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:16.600
Who will he use for this play?

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:28.370
<i>I won't let you shoot!</i>

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:30.450
<i>I've got to go with my left!</i>

00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:39.500
The middle, Aizawa, comes back 
with another explosive shot,

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:41.870
this time with a powerful left.

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:46.300
We are really getting to see what the 
FC's first year, Kakeru Aizawa, can do!

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:49.260
<i>His left is stronger than his right!</i>

00:13:49.810 --> 00:13:52.060
<i>His control is little shaky, though.</i>

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:54.520
<i>That's right, Suguru was a lefty.</i>

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:57.290
That was quite surprising,

00:13:57.290 --> 00:13:59.870
to think that Kakeru-kun 
had a left like that.

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:03.410
Until recently, Kakeru
 couldn't use his left leg.

00:14:03.850 --> 00:14:07.490
He was even going to quit during 
middle school because of it.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:11.200
However, since then he 
practiced every day and...

00:14:12.340 --> 00:14:13.660
Is that right?

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.080
This time it's Araki!

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:23.460
A long shot to wake you up.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:25.810
He aimed for the gap that 
the keeper had shown before,

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:27.790
but the ball flew just above the bar.

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:30.640
You can't let your guard 
down around this man.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:34.130
That guy gives me the chills.

00:14:34.130 --> 00:14:36.230
Todo, don't go too far forward.

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:38.090
We have to crush them early.

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:40.440
Be ready for them to 
attack from anywhere.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:41.440
Okay.

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:46.700
Coach, could this be...

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:49.740
Mishima-san, I see you've figured 
out what those two are planning.

00:14:57.320 --> 00:14:59.810
It's all middle and long shots.

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:01.580
What are they aiming for?

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:04.460
Mako-san!

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:06.310
Don't rush, Kakeru.

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:10.590
<i>The striker's stage.</i>

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:11.970
Here comes the middle.

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:14.760
<i>Now!</i>

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:24.730
I won't let you shoot!

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:29.650
<i>Why don't we get started?</i>

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:37.370
<i>Yours and mine,</i>

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.540
<i>our show without a scenario.</i>

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:41.620
No! Check number 9!

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:47.160
<i>Araki-san!</i>

00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:14.370
He's got it! He's got it!

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:17.110
A killer pass splits the field

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:19.820
and the one who receives it 
is the first year striker,

00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:21.120
Kakeru Aizawa!

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:46.040
Goooal!

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:49.030
It's finally reached 3-3, tie game!

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:53.450
FC has stepped up to take this game.

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:55.190
Kakeru!

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:56.660
It was nothing less than spectacular.

00:16:57.140 --> 00:17:00.470
The defensive line pulled 
forward to address the middle.

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:03.120
The keeper pulls back 
in fear of a long shot.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:06.580
A large space was created in that gap.

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:10.390
The hotline from the 
conductor to the striker...

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:13.930
Those two made a huge goal.

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:16.220
They got us.

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:17.100
Yeah...

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:18.610
But it's still a tie game.

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:19.850
Let's change our attitude and—

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:23.720
Sawamura-san, it's not enough 
just to change our attitude.

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:29.610
The three goals that we lost were all

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:32.150
fast pass work or careful technique.

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:34.150
They scored in the blink of an eye.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.200
Our defenses, which, 
up until now, had retreated

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.700
every time they took the ball,

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:42.120
can no longer stop their 
constantly changing attacks.

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:45.480
But, we can't change Coach 
Kondo's strategy now...

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:48.580
If we lose, we lose the 
right to play competitively.

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:51.300
I don't want to have any regrets.

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:53.380
If they take the ball,
 we need to take it right back

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.360
and stay in possession of the ball.

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:58.320
Sawamura-san, I need you 
to protect the front line.

00:17:58.320 --> 00:17:59.460
Oda...

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:07.810
All right.

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:10.880
There are 10 minutes left. 
We will have no regrets!

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:11.650
Right!

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:16.070
<i>Think.</i>

00:18:16.730 --> 00:18:17.960
<i>Think.</i>

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:20.990
<i>Don't just repeat what 
we do in practice.</i>

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:24.080
<i>Make the plays that 
we think of ourselves.</i>

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:37.970
Hiro, Kakeru, forecheck.

00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:42.900
Kakeru, take the middle.

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:44.630
Don't let Oda get a pass.

00:18:44.630 --> 00:18:45.830
Mako, back him up!

00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:50.660
Playing from a high position, 
assertively trying to steal the ball

00:18:50.660 --> 00:18:53.420
and increasing the chance for control.

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:56.360
This is how we, the FC, play soccer.

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:57.570
Teshigawara!

00:19:02.630 --> 00:19:04.370
Sawamura! It's all yours!

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:09.540
Matoba intercepts!

00:19:10.800 --> 00:19:11.790
Forecheck!

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:19.330
Kudo.

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:20.220
All right.

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:25.640
I won't let you by!

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:29.250
SC, who had fallen back as soon 
as the ball changed possession,

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:31.250
now goes into a quick check!

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:33.450
Have they changed strategy?

00:19:33.450 --> 00:19:36.450
There didn't appear to be 
any sign from Coach Kondo.

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:38.810
What could this mean?

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:44.780
Matoba slips a pass past Takase!

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:46.490
<i>He's...</i>

00:19:50.350 --> 00:19:51.500
Hino-san!

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:56.380
If it had gone through, 
 that would've been a decisive pass.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:58.550
Too bad. Kaiouji stops it.

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:12.390
Oda... What are you...

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:14.900
He dribbles.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.720
From the base of middle field,

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:18.290
Oda breaks into a dribble.

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:21.100
He breaks past one opponent and 
makes it to the halfway line.

00:20:21.100 --> 00:20:22.300
He's still going.

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:24.360
Is he going to take it 
all the way himself?

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:27.830
This is a surprising play we'd 
never expect Oda to make.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:29.540
You!

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:34.000
Hey, you! Don't you have to 
obey the bench's orders?

00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:40.880
If it's to win, I'll do anything.

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:43.220
Fine with me!

00:20:43.690 --> 00:20:45.830
I'll never let you have it.

00:20:45.830 --> 00:20:47.680
That's unfortunate.

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:53.710
Go! Go! Oda!

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:54.730
Araki-kun!

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:56.620
Oda against Araki,

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.870
a one-on-one between the two aces.

00:20:58.870 --> 00:21:00.410
In the match which had

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:02.230
depended on tactics between FC and SC,

00:21:02.230 --> 00:21:04.700
this is a spectacle we 
haven't seen before.

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:07.180
They're both amazing.

00:21:07.180 --> 00:21:09.350
I can feel my heart beating, Brother.

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:12.910
I haven't had a match 
this exciting in so long.

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:18.880
Oda!

00:21:21.820 --> 00:21:23.220
<i>A heel pass?</i>

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:28.800
It's the centerback, Kaiouji!

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:31.130
He's been on defense the entire time,

00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:33.140
but he's going for an overlap.

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:43.570
What?

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:46.070
No way! No way!

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:48.090
Oh, defeated!

00:21:48.090 --> 00:21:51.300
Horikawa sends the shot 
back with a sliding tackle.

00:21:51.300 --> 00:21:53.620
I'm impressed again and again

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:55.250
by this man's quick thinking.

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:01.100
We're in overtime.

00:22:01.100 --> 00:22:03.050
Five minutes have been added to the clock.

00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:07.510
Will the winning goal 
be scored by SC or by FC?

00:22:07.810 --> 00:22:11.300
Which team will represent Enoshima High?

00:22:11.300 --> 00:22:13.560
I cannot take my eyes 
off the intense plays

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:16.450
that both teams are making, 
even for a second.

00:22:25.920 --> 00:22:28.700
<i>We're going to win!</i>

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:33.450
A nice save by the goal 
keeper, Kurebayashi.

00:22:34.150 --> 00:22:37.870
Nakatsuka makes a gutsy play, 
a corner kick!

00:22:41.220 --> 00:22:43.000
I'll stop you this time!

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:45.420
Kakeru-kun!

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:47.730
Leave it to me!

00:22:49.870 --> 00:22:53.680
I won't let you play in 
the penalty area anymore!

00:22:55.380 --> 00:22:56.310
Hino-san!

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:03.210
This is amazing!

00:23:03.210 --> 00:23:04.910
It's dramatic and drastic

00:23:04.910 --> 00:23:06.150
and fantastic!

00:23:06.670 --> 00:23:09.810
Both teams are performing splendidly.

00:23:09.810 --> 00:23:12.580
I don't want either team to lose.

00:23:12.580 --> 00:23:14.060
That's how I feel as an 
Enoshima High student,

00:23:14.060 --> 00:23:15.540
from the bottom of my heart.

00:23:15.860 --> 00:23:18.540
Go SC! Go FC!

00:23:18.840 --> 00:23:21.500
Go! Go! Go!

00:23:25.200 --> 00:23:27.360
<i>How many minutes are left?</i>

00:23:32.920 --> 00:23:36.810
<i>The sound of my brother's 
heartbeat is ringing in my ears.</i>

00:23:40.910 --> 00:23:45.230
<i>My legs are heavy.
 It's like this isn't my body.</i>

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:51.640
Here it is!

00:23:51.640 --> 00:23:53.660
Araki's killer pass!

00:23:53.660 --> 00:23:55.110
This time to Matoba.

00:23:55.110 --> 00:23:57.290
Will this be the last attack?

00:23:58.190 --> 00:24:00.350
<i>But, for some reason...</i>

00:24:01.380 --> 00:24:02.750
<i>I want to keep going.</i>

00:24:09.160 --> 00:24:10.920
<i>I want to keep running.</i>

00:24:13.390 --> 00:24:15.900
<i>I want to keep playing 
this kind of soccer,</i>

00:24:17.180 --> 00:24:20.090
<i>keep playing with everyone.</i>

00:24:38.320 --> 00:24:43.060
What is this?!
 Kakeru Aizawa with an overhead!

00:24:45.940 --> 00:25:15.400
<b>Next Episode: Conclusion</b>

00:24:46.960 --> 00:24:49.960
At the end of the match, 
Kakeru hits an overhead.

00:24:50.470 --> 00:24:52.940
The fateful shot carries 
with it the future

00:24:52.940 --> 00:24:54.350
and hopes of his teammates.

00:24:54.840 --> 00:24:57.070
Is the cheer that resounds 
on the grounds,

00:24:57.070 --> 00:24:59.730
the ringing bell of redemption?

00:25:00.330 --> 00:25:02.640
That which is born 
following a fierce battle.

00:25:02.640 --> 00:25:04.040
With everyone's hopes on his chest,

00:25:04.040 --> 00:25:06.270
what path will Coach Iwaki choose?

00:25:06.530 --> 00:25:08.320
Next time on Knight in the Area,

00:25:08.320 --> 00:25:10.510
episode 8: "Conclusion."

00:25:10.910 --> 00:25:12.280
The ball's still in play!

00:25:12.280 --> 00:25:13.400
Run, Kakeru!
